            <title>[LU-21041] sanity-hsm test_251/254b: copytool .lustre/fid lookup ENOENT with 12 MDTs</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21041</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;Claude&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; With 12 MDTs, the sanity-hsm copytool cannot open files by FID: llapi_hsm_action_begin() on /mnt/lustre2/.lustre/fid/&amp;lt;FID&amp;gt; returns ENOENT for files that exist, so HSM requests never reach STARTED and test_251 and test_254b fail.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;sanity-hsm test_251: @@@@@@ FAIL: request on 0x20000040d:0xb5:0x0 is not STARTED on mds1
sanity-hsm test_254b: @@@@@@ FAIL: Expected 52 (!= 0) active archive requests
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Copytool log (lhsmtool_posix on onyx-155vm20, mounted on /mnt/lustre2), test_251:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;[0x20000040d:0xb5:0x0] action ARCHIVE reclen 72, cookie=0x6abb40ff
processing file 'd251.sanity-hsm/f251.sanity-hsm'
llapi_hsm_action_begin() on '/mnt/lustre2/.lustre/fid/0x20000040d:0xb5:0x0' failed: No such file or directory (2)
Action completed, notifying coordinator cookie=0x6abb40ff, FID=[0x20000040d:0xb5:0x0], hp_flags=0 err=2
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;test_254b shows the same ENOENT for every archive request (e.g. &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0x20000040d:0xb7:0x0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;). The files were created on /mnt/lustre on the other client in a directory created with mkdir_on_mdt0, and still exist.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Configuration: 2 MDS nodes, MDSCOUNT=12, from the custom test session for &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69303" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69303&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14058" title="Create tests for large number of MDTs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14058"&gt;LU-14058&lt;/a&gt; &amp;gt;10 MDT script fixes), which removes the old MDSCOUNT limit from sanity-hsm.sh. sanity-hsm has not previously been run with more than 10 MDTs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo auto-linked &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16932" title="sanity-hsm test_251: request on 0x200007938:0xc3:0x0 is not STARTED on mds1" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16932"&gt;LU-16932&lt;/a&gt; by error signature, but the cause here is the ENOENT FID lookup on the copytool mount, not a timing issue. Possibly the same root cause as the sanity-hsm test_500 failure with 12 MDTs (stat of a just-created directory returns ENOENT), see linked ticket.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity-hsm test_251 and test_254b are excluded with MDSCOUNT &amp;gt; 9 by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14058" title="Create tests for large number of MDTs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14058"&gt;LU-14058&lt;/a&gt; until this is fixed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
