                            <comment id="504439" author="adilger" created="Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:37:45 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;Claude&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; The diagnosis in this ticket's description was wrong; the copytool ENOENT is a side effect, not a .lustre/fid lookup failure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;test_251 is the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16932" title="sanity-hsm test_251: request on 0x200007938:0xc3:0x0 is not STARTED on mds1" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16932"&gt;LU-16932&lt;/a&gt; race: with active_request_timeout=1 the request stays STARTED for only about 1-2s, and wait_request_state polls about every 1.3s, so it saw WAITING then CANCELED ("Changed after 1s: from 'WAITING' to 'CANCELED'"). When the copytool then calls LL_IOC_HSM_COPY_START for the already-cancelled request, the MDS logs "mdt_hsm_update_request_state()) lustre-MDT0000: Cannot find running request for cookie 0x6abb40ff" and returns ENOENT.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;test_254b failed because test_251 restored active_request_timeout and loop_period only at the end of the test body, so after the failure both stayed at 1 and 254b's requests timed out before they could be counted.&lt;br/&gt;
Neither is specific to many MDTs. Resolving as a duplicate of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16932" title="sanity-hsm test_251: request on 0x200007938:0xc3:0x0 is not STARTED on mds1" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16932"&gt;LU-16932&lt;/a&gt;, where a test fix will be posted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
